guide.echoes_fireforge.forge.reforging.p:
To reforge, you need four things:

- the item, placed by hand;
- an offering, placed by hand, consumed by each reforge;
- a fuel, which sets the heat;
- water: one bottle per reforge.

Strike the hammer in the interface. A reforge takes about 10 seconds and replaces the previous rarity.

guide.echoes_fireforge.forge.heat.p1:
Heat comes from the fuel that is burning. It sets the highest possible rarity:

- wood, planks: Warm, Raw at best;
- coal: Hot, Tempered;
- coal block: Blazing, Refined;
- blaze rod: Searing, Stoked;
- lava: Furnace, Special possible.

A higher roll drops back to the cap. One fuel per reforge; a lava bucket lasts four.

guide.echoes_fireforge.forge.rarities.p1:
Each reforge rolls a rarity:

- Cracked: one malus (−2 to −6%);
- Raw: nothing;
- Tempered: one bonus (+1 to +3%);
- Refined: two bonuses (+2 to +6%);
- Stoked: two or three bonuses (+4 to +9%) and one drawback;
- Special: a unique effect and one drawback.

guide.echoes_fireforge.forge.offerings.p:
What you give to the fire. The offering improves the rarity odds, and gives a small chance of a rare enchantment, always compatible with the item:

- gold nugget, quartz: small boost;
- magma cream, ghast tear: good;
- netherite scrap: large.

The costlier the offering, the higher the chance.

guide.echoes_fireforge.forge.cracks.p1:
Each material has its limit:

- leather, wood, gold, bow, crossbow: Hot;
- stone, chainmail, iron, shield: Blazing;
- diamond, trident, mace: Searing;
- netherite: anything.

For each step beyond it, the forge cracks once during the reforge: it shakes, throws sparks, and the frame turns red.

guide.echoes_fireforge.forge.soul_module:
At a normal fire, souls pay for options:

- lock a bonus (15): it stays whatever happens;
- guarantee (20): no Cracked or Raw roll;
- reroll (10): keeps the rarity, rerolls the values, no fuel or offering.

Souls are paid when the hammer strikes.
